# pnpm allowBuilds

Never leave the placeholder string `set this to true or false` in `allowBuilds`. pnpm 10+ treats that as ignored lifecycle scripts and fails install with `ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS`.

For this Next.js app, native binaries must be allowed:

```yaml
allowBuilds:
  sharp: true
  unrs-resolver: true
  msw: false
  "@parcel/watcher": true
  "@swc/core": true
```

- `@swc/core` — Next compile (dev + build)
- `@parcel/watcher` — `next dev` file watching
- `sharp` and `unrs-resolver` stay `true`; `msw` stays `false`
- Edit `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, then `pnpm i`. Do not use the interactive TUI `pnpm approve-builds`.
- Package manager: `pnpm` / `pnpx` only. No `npm`, `npx`, or `curl`.
